+## 5. Proposed Reviewed Fix (For Post-Diagnostic Implementation)
+
+To address all confirmed authority defects without modifying production source during this diagnostic phase, the following reviewed changes are proposed for [library_mirror.py](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom\worktrees\uoink-library\213914a5-528\gemini/library_mirror.py):
+
+### 1. Enforce Creation Order and Parent Liveness in `owned_pids()`
+```python
+# In _VaultIoSession.owned_pids():
+# Only enumerate Toolhelp children if self.pid is confirmed alive and matches self.created_ms
+if os.name == "nt" and self.pid and _pid_is_alive(self.pid, self.created_ms):
+    parent_created = self.created_ms or _process_created_ms(self.pid)
+    for child in _windows_process_children(self.pid):
+        exe = str(child.get("exe") or "")
+        if _is_console_host(exe):
+            continue
+        child_pid = int(child["pid"])
+        child_created = _process_created_ms(child_pid)
+        # Discard any orphan created before the parent
+        if parent_created is not None and child_created is not None:
+            if child_created < (parent_created - _PROCESS_START_TOLERANCE_MS):
+                continue
+        add(child_pid, exe, created=child_created)
+```
+
+### 2. Latch Confirmed Process Death to Prevent Exit Amnesia
+```python
+# In _VaultIoSession.__init__():
+self._dead_pids: set[int] = set()
+
+# In _VaultIoSession.physical_liveness():
+# If proc.poll() confirmed death, latch self.pid as dead and do not query by raw PID
+if proc is not None:
+    try:
+        poll = proc.poll()
+    except Exception:
+        states.append("unknown")
+    else:
+        if poll is None:
+            return "alive"
+        if self.pid:
+            self._dead_pids.add(self.pid)
+
+# When checking writer_pid and owned PIDs, skip latched dead PIDs
+for pid, created in list(self._owned_created.items()):
+    if pid in self._dead_pids:
+        states.append("dead")
+        continue
+    status = _process_liveness(pid, created)
+    if status == "dead":
+        self._dead_pids.add(pid)
+    states.append(status)
+```
+
+### 3. Handle `GetProcessTimes` Failure in `_process_liveness`
+```python
+# In _process_liveness:
+if created_ms is not None:
+    actual = _windows_process_created_ms(handle)
+    if actual is None:
+        # Cannot confirm identity; must not fall through to "alive"
+        return "unknown"
+    if abs(actual - int(created_ms)) > _PROCESS_START_TOLERANCE_MS:
+        return "dead"
+```
+
+These changes:
+1. Retain unknown-child exclusion (unverified children remain unknown).
+2. Retain late-write refusal (dead sessions remain dead).
+3. Retain destination-alias safety (gate locks remain keyed to destination identity).
+4. Retain independent user bytes (stale sessions cannot write).
+5. Release admission after known death (confirmed death is latched and cannot revert to alive).
